{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792246297,"nonce":"+6JXRiOo/zcjFJVH7yBD67lt5A0=","title":"HashLink programs cannot bring their own fonts","message":"**What**\n\nblinc_abi decodes bundled faces in font.rs but HashLink has no primitive to hand it font bytes, so text is set only in fonts the system has. A program in a page, where the host has no system fonts, cannot set any text.\n\n**Fix**\n\nhl_blinc_font_register takes TTF, OpenType, collection or WOFF2 bytes and adds their faces to blinc_text's registry (load_font_data), found by the family names they carry, then clears the cached generic-family misses so a generic family can find them.\n\n**Limit**\n\nblinc_text caches a failed lookup of a family name, and has no way to clear those, so a font must be registered before any text is laid out in its family. Generic families fall back to a short list of names (Roboto, Noto Sans, DejaVu Sans, JetBrains Mono, Fira Code and others), so a program bundling one of those has working generics.\n\nNeeded by ashui's wasm work (ashui git-bug 0c8c9a02fd454598cd2c6416e34a2595bb562a525a8e14d298084a672907ed68).","files":null}]}